<?xml version="1.0"?>
<CP_Scriptfile date="Jun 30, 2022">
<CPscript title="Discrete Error Function Example" level="min" screenmode="map" >
<description>We construct a discrete version of the classical error function, erf(z). By adding a generation of circles at a time in the domain, one can see the development of the logarithmic branching at 1 and -1 in the range, the asmyptotic behavior, and the multi-sheeted covering behavior. These are all faithful to the behavior of erf(z) itself.</description>
<text> A hex domain is loaded in p0. Press 'e' to apply the 'error function' construction, creating the image in p1; this involves setting the boundary radii in p1 based on the value of the error function at the centers in p0, then repacking p1, laying it out, and displaying it with boundary circles shaded. Press 'a' to add a new generation to p0, then 'e' to compute the new image. Press '1' to focus p1 in at the logarithmic branching occurring at z=1; press '2' to pull back for a view of the full packing. </text>
<cmd name="*" mnemonic="*" tooltip="Start over" iconname="debugger.png">act 0;Cleanse;create hex 3;gamma 8;set_rad .1 a;layout;set_screen -h 4.0;Disp -w -c -cf b;set_cycles 10000; </cmd>
<cmd iconname="xeyes.png">[e]; </cmd>
<cmd iconname="kivio.png">[a]; </cmd>
<cmd iconname="metacontact_online.png">[e]; </cmd>
<text> It is left to the reader to investigate the properties of this function and the questions posed in Section 6.5.3. Among other things, try to watch the evolving behavior of the boundary circles as you add generations. </text>
<Section title="Tools">
<cmd inline="no" name="e" mnemonic="e" tooltip="Apply the error function, repack, display p1" iconname="xeyes.png">act 1;erf_ftn 0 1 2;set_aim -d;repack -p1;layout -p1;set_screen -h 4.0;Disp -p1 -w -c -cf b; </cmd>
<cmd inline="no" name="a" mnemonic="a" tooltip="Add a new generation" iconname="network.png">add_gen -p0 1 6;layout -p0;set_screen -h 4.0;Disp -p0 -w -c -cf b; </cmd>
<cmd inline="no" name="1" mnemonic="1" tooltip="Focus in at z=1 in the image" iconname="debugger.png">focus -p1 -z 1.0 0.0;set_screen -p1 -h .1;disp -p1 -wr; </cmd>
<cmd inline="no" name="2" mnemonic="2" tooltip="Move back for global view" iconname="delete.png">set_screen -p1 -a;disp -p1 -wr; </cmd>
</Section>
  </CPscript>
<CPdata>
    <AboutImage name="AboutImage.jpg">

    </AboutImage>
  </CPdata>
</CP_Scriptfile>
